Did you get "No  write permission to lock perm!"? If so, it's a bug and
the fix can be got at the bottom of: 
http://www.nethack.org/v343/ports/download-mac.html 

Otherwise, make sure that 1. the free space reported is >0 (even if
used<total sometimes there is a difference as in *nix for example) 2.
you *did* login as games and ran recover <lockfile perfix> in the lib
directory i.e. if you have a bunch of very recent files called alock.1
alock.2  etc then you would type recover alock *in* *that* *directory*.
3. you aren't using a recent version of slash'em as opposed to nethack
(doesn't do it separately - recovers automatically). Any other
conditions along these lines would be helpful. Don't start another game
or copy those alock files elsewhere, or the recovery is gone forever.

